  "body": "Please consider adding the ports used for Microsoft's SMB and NetBIOS protocols (137, 445, possibly others; 139 is already blacklisted) to the \"bad port\" blacklist.  This is prompted by the [MS17-010](https://github.com/RiskSense-Ops/MS17-010) exploit, but there's quite a long history of remotely exploitable SMB bugs.  This will, at least, make it harder to [scan for exploitable systems](http://www.andlabs.org/tools/jsrecon/jsrecon.html) from a malicious website.",
